WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.470
Ant-Man And The Wasp's post-credit scenes
finally answer the question: where was Ant-Man

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.030
in Avengers: Infinity War?

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:11.200
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the two post-credits

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.160
scenes in Ant-Man And The Wasp, explaining
their connection to Infinity War and how they

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.570
set us up for Avengers 4.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:21.840
If you're new here, I do regular superhero
videos plus I'm kicking off a new Marvel giveaway.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.100
Make sure you're subscribed and leave a comment
about the movie to enter.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.600
Spoilers ahead for Ant-Man And The Wasp and
Infinity War.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.020
The mid-credits scene opens with Scott Lang
preparing to head back into the Quantum Realm

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.940
on a mission to collect quantum healing particles.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.640
Janet van Dyne warns Scott to stay away from
Tardigrades and not to get sucked into a time

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.870
vortex.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.000
Once inside the Quantum Realm, Scott collects
some healing particles, then reports he's

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.579
ready to come back.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:54.250
Hope counts down his return over the mic 5...
4... 3... but then the line goes dead.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.359
As the camera cuts back to where Hope, Janet
and Hank were operating the Quantum tunnel,

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:02.940
we see the remains of 3 clouds of ash falling
to little piles on the floor.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.750
Basically, the Pym family has been dusted
by Thanos's snap at the end of Avengers: Infinity

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:08.750
War.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.189
It's a really ominous moment when you hear
Scott's panicked voice over the mic as the

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:14.700
camera pans through little clouds of ash.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.220
He realises something's wrong but has no idea
what.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.520
The scene is also a chilling reminder of the
Infinity War post-credits scene where Nick

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.149
Fury and Maria Hill evaporated into ash in
New York.

00:01:26.149 --> 00:01:30.200
It's especially tough to watch as Hope only
suited up as the Wasp in this movie.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.570
And Janet van Dyne was only just rescued from
the Quantum Realm, and now we have to see

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.890
them dusted.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:40.469
Wasp will be in Avengers 4, however, Evangeline
Lilly has said she's only going to be in it

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:44.260
a little which is disappointing as it seems
she'll probably be limited to just scenes

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.610
where she returns with the other dusted heroes.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:51.750
Now, there is a glimmer of hope no pun intended
in Janet's last words to Scott about time

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.760
vortices in the Quantum Realm.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.149
Avengers 4 is very likely to be set several
years after the snap in a film that I expect

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:02.079
will show the surviving Avengers adjusting
to a decimated world and figuring out what

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:03.729
they can do about it.

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:08.560
Marvel has cast a currently 16-year old Emma
Fuhrmann to play an older version of Scott's

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.599
daughter Cassie in Avengers 4, which means,
I expect, that once Scott realises that there's

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.950
no one at the other end in the real world
to bring him back, he may try travelling through

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.450
a time vortex.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.159
This could take him into the future where
he meets an older Cassie and then together

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:26.310
they visit Tony Stark to tell him about the
Quantum Realm, and the Avengers then try to

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.840
figure out how they can use time travel to
fix what Thanos did.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.799
This would tie in with the Avengers 4 set
photos of Ant-Man in New York with Iron Man

00:02:33.799 --> 00:02:38.730
and Captain America with each of them wearing
a similar looking device around their wrist.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.819
Another possibility for how Scott escapes
from the Quantum Realm could tie in with Captain

00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:43.819
Marvel.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:48.150
I expect a reason will be revealed in her
film as to why Carol Danvers hasn't been around

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.540
or available during the various crises we've
seen on Earth, such as the Battle of New York,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.160
Sokovia, or Infinity War itself.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.049
It could be that she's in the Quantum Realm
herself.

00:02:58.049 --> 00:03:02.129
And the beeper that Nick Fury set off to contact
her in the Infinity War post-credits scene

00:03:02.129 --> 00:03:04.879
may be able to communicate with Carol there.

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:07.820
Ant-Man might hear the beeper while he's stuck
there too.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.090
And he and Carol might both even meet up in
a Captain Marvel post-credits scene that sets

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:14.970
them up to meet the Avengers in Avengers 4.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:19.269
Another possibility is that Scott simply gets
stuck in the Quantum Realm for several years

00:03:19.269 --> 00:03:22.939
and learns new secrets and survives there,
just like Janet did.

00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:26.800
His daughter Cassie could eventually find
out where the mobile Quantum tunnel was located

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.250
and so she turns it on again to bring him
back out.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.000
What's also interesting in this credits scene
is that Scott was collecting Quantum healing

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.000
particles.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.939
These were being gathered to help Ghost, however,
there's a chance they could also play a role

00:03:38.939 --> 00:03:42.319
in restoring the heroes who were dusted in
the Thanos snap.

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:46.329
There is a second post-credits scene which,
while short, does provide a little more backdrop

00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:48.079
for Avengers 4.

00:03:48.079 --> 00:03:52.610
After all the credits have rolled, we snap
back to Scott's house which seems to be deserted.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:56.739
Everything is quiet except for the dissonant
tone of an emergency broadcast playing on

00:03:56.739 --> 00:04:01.280
a TV screen, indicating the Thanos snap has
truly kicked off a crisis.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.560
This sense of unease is followed with a shot
of the ant who filled in for Scott during

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.390
his house arrest playing the drums.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:10.470
It's an uncomfortable moment watching the
ant drumming away as he seems oblivious to

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.360
the catastrophe around him.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.180
And just to unsettle us even further, as the
screen fades to black, a title card pops up

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:21.620
with the words "Ant-Man and the Wasp will
return", but a little question mark is added

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.150
after a second or two.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.810
We can't take this last bit too seriously
as I think Marvel is just gently trolling

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.930
us because as I said earlier, it's already
been confirmed that Evangeline Lilly does

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.770
return in Avengers 4.

